  "scenes": [
    {
      "narration": "In a crisis, America quietly lends trillions of dollars to other countries' central banks. It sounds generous. It isn't.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "hook",
          "art": "moneyFlow",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "bill"
          ],
          "lines": [
            "It bails out",
            "the world."
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s1"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The tool is called a dollar swap line, and the Fed opens them when the world runs short of dollars.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "truth",
          "art": "bank",
          "kicker": "the mechanic",
          "line": "Dollar swap lines",
          "sub": "the Fed lends dollars abroad"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s2"
    },
    {
      "narration": "A central bank liquidity swap exists to provide dollars to other central banks.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-swap",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · liquidity swap"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s3"
    },
    {
      "narration": "Why does the Fed care? Because about half of all world trade is invoiced in dollars.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "globe",
          "big": "~50%",
          "label": "of world trade is in dollars",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "bill"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s4"
    },
    {
      "narration": "The dollar's role as the reserve currency is America's greatest financial asset.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-exorbitant",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · exorbitant privilege"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s5"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So when foreign banks can't get dollars, the whole system that props up America is at risk.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "center",
          "art": "globeX",
          "line": "Protect the system",
          "props": [
            "globe",
            "fire"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s6"
    },
    {
      "narration": "In effect, the Fed becomes the lender of last resort for the entire planet.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "evidence",
          "sourceId": "wiki-lolr",
          "kicker": "Wikipedia · lender of last resort"
        }
      ],
      "id": "s7"
    },
    {
      "narration": "At the two thousand eight peak, those swap lines topped five hundred eighty billion dollars.",
      "shots": [
        {
          "block": "stat",
          "art": "bank",
          "big": "$580B+",
          "label": "Fed swap lines, 2008 peak",
          "props": [
            "bill",
            "bill"
          ]
        }
      ],
      "id": "s8"
    },
    {
      "narration": "So is it charity, or pure self-interest?",
      "shots": [
